Balancing Rover Telemetry",description:"IMU-based stabilization with live battery and tilt stats on OLED.",prompt:"Create an ESP32 self-balancing mini rover controller with an MPU6050 and OLED display. I need PID balancing logic, live tilt and battery telemetry on the OLED, and clear pin assignments.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-self-balancing-rover.webp"},{id:"kids-phone",category:"Communication",title:"ESP32 Kids Phone",description:"A kid-safe mini phone with big buttons, approved contacts, and SOS mode.",prompt:"Design an ESP32-based kids phone prototype with a small screen, 4x4 keypad, speaker, microphone, and simple menu UI. Include approved contacts only, an SOS shortcut button, call/voice-message style interaction, and battery status display.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-kids-phone.webp"},{id:"wearable",category:"Wearables",title:"Fitness Wristband Prototype",description:"Heart-rate sampling, step estimate, and low-power status display.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 wearable prototype with MAX30102 heart-rate sensor, MPU6050 motion tracking, and a small OLED. Show code for sampling, basic step estimation, and low-power behavior between updates.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-fitness-wristband.webp"},{id:"pico-cosmic-critter",category:"Pico Playground",title:"Pico Cosmic Critter",description:"A tiny alien pet with tilt moods, nebula lights, and chirpy sounds.",prompt:"Build a Raspberry Pi Pico cosmic critter pet using an MPU6050, WS2812B LED ring, OLED display, buzzer, and one button. Tilting the device should change the pet mood (happy, dizzy, sleepy, excited), update colors and face text, and play short chirps.",platform:"raspberry-pi-pico",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-cosmic-critter-pet.webp"},{id:"clawdbot-tamagotchi",category:"Companion Bot",title:"ClawdBot Tamagochi",description:"A tiny lobster-bot pet with moods, needs, and hatch-to-molt personality loops.",prompt:"Create an ESP32 ClawdBot Tamagochi-style companion bot with a lobster-themed OLED face, hatch/start flow, mood states (happy, hungry, sleepy, bored), feed/play/sleep actions via buttons, buzzer sound effects, and a care loop that makes the bot cranky if neglected and calmer when cared for.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-clawdbot-tamagotchi.webp"},{id:"arcade-reaction-tower",category:"Games",title:"Arcade Reaction Tower",description:"Fast reflex game with score tracking, LED flashes, and victory sounds.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 arcade reaction game with a WS2812 LED ring, one arcade button, buzzer, and OLED score display. I want random light cues, reaction-time scoring, and a short victory animation.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-arcade-reaction-tower.webp"},{id:"laser-harp-synth",category:"Music",title:"Laser Harp Synth",description:"Break light beams to trigger notes and visual feedback.",prompt:"Create an ESP32 laser harp synth using three laser/LDR channels, a piezo speaker, and OLED screen. Breaking each beam should play a different note and show the active note on display.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-laser-harp-synth.webp"},{id:"laser-security-demo",category:"Security",title:"Laser Tripwire Alarm Demo",description:"A classroom-safe beam-break alarm with an LDR, 10k resistor, buzzer, and status serial output.",prompt:"Build an Arduino Uno laser tripwire alarm demo using a laser pointer or low-power laser module, an LDR with a 10k resistor voltage divider, and a piezo buzzer. When the beam is broken, sound the buzzer and print an intruder-detected alert over Serial. Keep it scoped as a demo, not a real security system.",platform:"arduino-uno",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-laser-tripwire-alarm-demo.webp"},{id:"treasure-chest-rfid",category:"Adventure",title:"RFID Treasure Chest",description:"Tap the right tag to unlock a servo latch with dramatic effects.",prompt:"Design an ESP32 RFID treasure chest with MFRC522 reader, servo lock, buzzer, and OLED status text. Valid tag unlocks the chest and plays a success tune; invalid tags trigger warning beeps.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-rfid-treasure-chest.webp"},{id:"plant-disco-guardian",category:"Weird & Fun",title:"Plant Disco Guardian",description:"A plant monitor that celebrates watering with lights and sound.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 plant guardian using a soil moisture sensor, WS2812 LEDs, and buzzer. When the plant is dry, alert softly; when watered, play a disco celebration animation.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-plant-disco-guardian.webp"},{id:"rocket-launch-alarm",category:"Time & Fun",title:"Rocket Launch Alarm",description:"Morning alarm with countdown, launch lights, and liftoff sound.",prompt:"Create an ESP32 rocket-launch alarm clock with DS3231 RTC, WS2812 LEDs, and buzzer. At alarm time, run a 10-second countdown animation and then a liftoff sound/light sequence.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-rocket-launch-alarm-clock.webp"},{id:"focus-timer",category:"Productivity",title:"ESP32 Focus Timer",description:"Pomodoro-style work and break timer with OLED status, buzzer alerts, and a rotary control.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 Pomodoro focus timer using an SSD1306 OLED, KY-040 rotary encoder, piezo buzzer, and WS2812B LED ring. I want adjustable work and break sessions, pause/resume from the encoder button, visual progress feedback, and clear wiring, code, and libraries.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-focus-timer.webp"},{id:"weather-station",category:"Smart Home",title:"ESP32 Weather Station",description:"Fetch Amsterdam forecast data over Wi-Fi and show simple clothing advice on a colour LCD.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 weather station using Wi-Fi to fetch forecast data for Amsterdam from an API that does not require a key. Display the temperature and simple clothing advice on a Waveshare 1.83-inch LCD Rev2 with a 240x280 resolution. Use a minimal black-background UI and include wiring, code, libraries, and deploy steps.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-weather-station.webp"},{id:"chess-cyd",category:"Gaming",title:"Touchscreen Chess on a Cheap Yellow Display",description:"Run a playable touchscreen chess game with a local ESP32 opponent on the ESP32-2432S028R.",prompt:"Build a touchscreen chess game for an ESP32-2432S028R Cheap Yellow Display. Use the onboard ILI9341 TFT display and XPT2046 resistive touchscreen, draw an 8x8 chess board, handle touch selection and legal moves, and include a simple local AI opponent that can run on the ESP32.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-touchscreen-chess-game-on-a-cheap-yellow-display.webp"},{id:"led-matrix-message-board",category:"Smart Home",title:"LED Matrix Message Board",description:"Scroll custom messages across a cascaded dot matrix display.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 scrolling message board using a MAX7219 8x32 LED dot matrix module. I want smooth scrolling text with multiple configurable messages that cycle automatically. Include wiring, code, and libraries.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-led-matrix-message-board.webp"},{id:"co2-room-monitor",category:"Smart Home",title:"CO2 Room Monitor",description:"Track true CO2, temperature, and humidity on an OLED with clear ventilation warnings.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 room CO2 monitor with an Adafruit SCD41 sensor and SSD1306 OLED. Show CO2 ppm, temperature, humidity, and a warning when the room needs ventilation. Use I2C on GPIO21/GPIO22 and include wiring, code, libraries, and calibration notes.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-co2-room-monitor.webp"},{id:"air-quality-monitor",category:"Smart Home",title:"ESP32 Air Quality Monitor",description:"Read indoor temperature, humidity, and pressure with a comfort label on OLED.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 air quality monitor using a BME280 temperature/humidity/pressure sensor and an SSD1306 OLED display on a shared I2C bus. Show live readings and a simple comfort status. Include wiring, code, and libraries.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-air-quality-monitor.webp"},{id:"morning-thermal-printer",category:"Smart Home",title:"Morning Thermal Printer",description:"Daily briefing slip: Open-Meteo weather, Google Calendar events, and to-do lines on a CSN-A2 printer.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 daily briefing printer with a CSN-A2 thermal receipt printer on UART2 (GPIO 4 TX to printer RX, optional GPIO 5 RX at 9600 baud). After Wi-Fi connects, sync NTP time, fetch Open-Meteo weather and Google Calendar events for today, then print a formatted briefing with date, weather, appointments, and checkbox to-do lines. Use Adafruit Thermal Printer and ArduinoJson; power VH from a separate 5–9 V supply; deep sleep after printing.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-morning-thermal-printer.webp"},{id:"esp32-security-camera",category:"Security",title:"ESP32 Security Camera",description:"Stream a tiny ESP32-CAM over your local Wi-Fi network.",prompt:"Build an ESP32-CAM security camera that streams captures over local Wi-Fi. Use a USB programmer adapter for upload, include Wi-Fi placeholders, AI Thinker ESP32-CAM camera pin settings, browser-view code, setup steps, and safety notes for keeping the stream private.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-security-camera.webp"},{id:"esp32-video-doorbell",category:"Security",title:"ESP32 Video Doorbell",description:"Local Wi-Fi camera feed with a physical doorbell button, ring counter, status LED, and chime.",prompt:"Build an ESP32-CAM video doorbell with a local Wi-Fi live-view page, a momentary button on GPIO13, a passive buzzer chime on GPIO14, the onboard flash LED on GPIO4 for ring feedback, AI Thinker camera pin settings, safe 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi setup, complete wiring, and notes about keeping the stream private.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-video-doorbell.webp"},{id:"desk-presence-busy-light",category:"Productivity",title:"Desk Presence Busy Light",description:"Show free, present, or busy desk status with motion sensing, OLED text, and a colour ring.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 desk presence busy light using an HC-SR501 PIR motion sensor, SSD1306 OLED, WS2812B LED ring, and a manual busy button. Show free, present, and busy states with clear wiring, code, and tuning notes.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-desk-presence-busy-light.webp"},{id:"voice-controlled-robot-face",category:"Robotics",title:"Voice-Controlled Robot Face",description:"Build an ESP32-S3 robot face starter with display wiring, Wi-Fi control code, and calibration notes for turning a board into a character.",prompt:"Build a voice-controlled ESP32-S3 robot face with a small colour display, Wi-Fi control page, clear calibration notes, and room to add microphone, speaker, and servo behaviours as the character evolves.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-voice-controlled-robot-face.webp"},{id:"tiny-oled-desk-command-centre",category:"Smart Home",title:"Tiny OLED Desk Command Centre",description:"Build an ESP32 OLED desk display with Wi-Fi, weather, time, local IP printing, and a browser page for sending messages to the screen.",prompt:"Build a tiny ESP32 OLED desk command centre using an SSD1306 display. It should connect to Wi-Fi, show time and weather, print its local IP, host a small web page, and let me send a message that stays visible on the OLED for a few seconds.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-tiny-oled-desk-command-centre.webp"},{id:"sports-gps-hotspot",category:"Vehicles",title:"Sports GPS Hotspot",description:"Build a compact ESP32-C3 GPS hotspot that serves a live local dashboard for outdoor speed and location checks.",prompt:"Build a compact ESP32-C3 GPS tracker using a NEO-6M module and LiPo battery. It should create its own SportsGPS Wi-Fi hotspot and serve a live dashboard at 192.168.4.1 for speed, fix status, and location data.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-sports-gps-hotspot.webp"},{id:"pocket-gps-dashboard",category:"Vehicles",title:"Pocket GPS Dashboard",description:"Build an ESP32 GPS tracker with NEO-6M, LiPo charging, status LED, and a local Wi-Fi dashboard for live outdoor stats.",prompt:"Build a portable ESP32 GPS tracker with a NEO-6M module, LiPo battery, TP4056 charger, status LED, and a local Wi-Fi dashboard that shows GPS lock, speed, distance, and live movement stats from my phone.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-pocket-gps-dashboard.webp"},{id:"esp32-cam-setup-portal-security-camera",category:"Security",title:"ESP32-CAM Setup Portal Security Camera",description:"Build an ESP32-CAM security camera with a setup access point, local Wi-Fi configuration page, live camera mode, and power-cycle recovery.",prompt:"Build an ESP32-CAM security camera that boots into a setup portal, lets me enter Wi-Fi details from a browser, joins the saved network, keeps the flash LED off, streams locally, and can reset back to setup mode with repeated power cycles.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-cam-setup-portal-security-camera.webp"},{id:"hermes-voice-satellite",category:"Smart Home",title:"Hermes Voice Satellite",description:"A Nest Mini-style mic and speaker puck for local-network agent voice chats.",prompt:"Build an ESP32-S3 voice satellite with an INMP441 I2S microphone, MAX98357A I2S amplifier, push-to-talk button, and status LED. It should record a short WAV clip, send it to a local Hermes/OpenClaw voice bridge over Wi-Fi, and play back the synthesized reply through the speaker. Include LAN safety notes and clear bridge/API assumptions.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-a-hermes-voice-satellite.webp"},{id:"pet-treat-dispenser",category:"Pets",title:"ESP32 Pet Treat Dispenser",description:"Servo-fed treats with a measured bowl check and OLED status.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 pet treat dispenser using an HX711 load cell, a hobby servo gate, SSD1306 OLED, manual dispense button, and piezo buzzer. Include safe servo power guidance, bowl weight checks, cooldown logic, wiring, code, and libraries.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-pet-treat-dispenser.webp"},{id:"esp32-bluetooth-speaker",category:"Music",title:"ESP32 Bluetooth Speaker",description:"Stream phone audio over Bluetooth to a PCM5102A DAC, XH-A232 amplifier, speakers, and OLED visualizer.",prompt:"Build an ESP32 Bluetooth speaker using a PCM5102A I2S DAC, XH-A232 TPA3110 stereo amplifier, MP1584 buck converter, 12V adapter, two passive speakers, and SSD1306 OLED visualizer. Include Bluetooth A2DP sink firmware, I2S wiring on GPIO26/GPIO25/GPIO22, XSMT on GPIO27, OLED I2C on GPIO21/GPIO23, safe 12V-to-5V power guidance, complete assembly steps, and troubleshooting for DATA vs DIN on the DAC module.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/guide-thumbnails/build-an-esp32-bluetooth-speaker.webp"},{id:"esp32-digital-hair-clip",category:"Wearables",title:"Digital Hair Clip",description:"A wearable LilyGo T-Display that cycles through messages, clipped into your hair like a barrette.",prompt:"Build the viral digital hair clip on a LilyGo T-Display, the original ESP32 version also sold as the TTGO T-Display V1.1. It is not the T-Display-S3 and not the TTGO T1. The board has a built-in 1.14 inch ST7789 135x240 colour display, used at rotation 1 so the usable screen is 240x135. Use the Arduino_GFX_Library (moononournation/GFX Library for Arduino) with Arduino_ESP32SPI on TFT_SCLK 18, TFT_MOSI 19, TFT_CS 5, TFT_DC 16, TFT_RST 23 and backlight TFT_BL 4. Cycle through a short array of messages drawn in large centred white text on black. The top button on GPIO 35 steps to the next message; the bottom button on GPIO 0 blanks the screen and enters deep sleep, and wakes the board again via ext0 on the same pin. Shrink the text to fit the screen and only scroll a message when it would have to drop below text size 2. Include LiPo battery polarity and safety notes for the Micro JST 1.25mm connector, the optional proto-board backing with female headers, and gluing the barrette to the flat plate rather than the hinge.",platform:"esp32",thumbnail:"/blog/digital-hair-clip/hero-youtube-thumbnail.webp"}];a.map(e=>e.id)},80079:(e,t,n)=>{function a(){return!!window.matchMedia?.("(pointer: coarse)")?.matches}function r(e,t=!1){return"Enter"===e.key&&!e.shiftKey&&!e.isComposing&&(!t||!!(e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey))}n.d(t,{G:()=>r,T:()=>a})},80397:(e,t,n)=>{n.d(t,{KR:()=>a,Z5:()=>r}),n(27714);let a=["undefined_symbol","api_mismatch","missing_header_or_library","malformed_code","firmware_too_large","board_configuration_failure","dependency_install_failure","missing_compile_diagnostic","compiler_failure","linker_failure","unsafe_include","infrastructure_failure","unknown_compile_failure"];function r(e){if(!e||"object"!=typeof e||Array.isArray(e))return"";for(let t of[e.compileDiagnostic,e.logs,e.error,e.message])if("string"==typeof t&&t.trim())return t;return""}},80648:(e,t,n)=>{n.d(t,{Z:()=>s});var a=n(57678),r=n(13698);let i=["build","simulate","code","openProjects","newPrompt","openDeploy","versionHistory","supportingFiles","keyboardShortcuts","focusChat"];function s(e,t={}){let[n,l]=(0,a.useState)(!1),o=(0,a.useMemo)(()=>e,[e]),d=(0,a.useCallback)(e=>{if((0,r.UJ)(e,r.e.leaveTextInput)&&(0,r.$g)(e.target))return void e.target.blur();if(l(e.ctrlKey),!(!e.ctrlKey||(0,r.$g)(e.target)))for(let n of i){let a=o[n]??("focusChat"===n&&t.focusChatRef?()=>t.focusChatRef?.current?.focus():void 0);if(a&&(0,r.UJ)(e,r.e[n])){e.preventDefault(),a(e);return}}},[t.focusChatRef,o]);return(0,a.useEffect)(()=>{let e=e=>{e.ctrlKey||l(!1)},t=()=>l(!1);return window.addEventListener("keydown",d),window.addEventListener("keyup",e),window.addEventListener("blur",t